From 9e8789bd2c3c89ed144b53e1a4b0c1aff0497996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@Averys-MacBook-Air.local>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:28:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] MoltenVK: fewer render pass ends and cheaper per-draw
 root state

- Buffer transitions between read-only states no longer end the render pass on MoltenVK (COMMON,
  INDIRECT_ARGUMENT, acceleration structures and buffers with pending RTAS work still do).
- CopyDescriptors on the vkUpdateDescriptorSets path copies only the runs of descriptors each set uses, and a
  whole call goes out as one vkUpdateDescriptorSets.
- Root addresses, dirty root constants and table offsets are gathered into one shadow block and pushed with one
  vkCmdPushConstants per draw/dispatch; runs of adjacent dirty descriptor sets bind with one call.
- CopyBufferRegion from an UPLOAD-heap buffer on a direct list goes into a per-list command buffer submitted just
  before the list (with a barrier at its end) instead of ending the render pass, and consecutive copies between
  the same buffers merge into one multi-region copy (on by default on MoltenVK; VKD3D_CONFIG=no_hoist_upload_copies
  turns it off, hoist_upload_copies turns it on elsewhere).
- Static descriptor-table CBVs are hoisted to push descriptors on MoltenVK, where Metal's constant buffers read
  1.5-1.7x faster, capped at 8 per root signature (VKD3D_CONFIG=no_hoist_table_cbv / hoist_table_cbv).
- New allocations on MoltenVK count as already zeroed, so no GPU clear submit is made for them.

Measured on an M4 MacBook Air with the matching MoltenVK changes: God of War Ragnarok 25-30 -> a steady 40 fps
(its frame limit). Targeted d3d12 tests (64) match the unmodified build.
